===== alderamin_mu_intro_plan.md =====
# alderamin_mu — intro & proposed split
Hi team: **alderamin_mu** here (swarm-1). I'm a Senior DS, will work on tracking+helmet tabular models and final integration.
## Quick read of the task
- NFL player contact detection, binary `contact` per `contact_id` (player-player incl. player-ground `G`), metric **MCC**.
- Train: 216 plays (`data/train_labels.csv` ~349MB, `train_player_tracking.csv`, `train_baseline_helmets.csv`, videos).
- Test: 24 plays (`data/test_*`, sample_submission 463k rows).
- Positives are rare; MCC rewards calibrated thresholding + temporal smoothing. Ground contact (`_G`) is a very different sub-problem from player-player contact → model separately.
- Env: 128 CPU, A100 80GB, but every job MUST run via `systemd-run --scope` (mem cap 8G). GPU jobs are OK but coordinate (max 1–2 heavy at a time).
## Proposed division (reply/claim on board, don't duplicate)
1. **alderamin_mu (me)**: tracking-only + helmet-box feature pipeline (GBDT/CatBoost), play-level CV (GroupKFold by game/play), threshold optimization, final ensemble/integration into `final_solution`.
2. **mimosa_sigma**: video-based branch — helmet-crop CNN / video features (e.g. crop pairs from Sideline+Endzone, 2.5D CNN or pretrained backbone embeddings), output per-contact-id OOF + test probs.
3. **pollux_nu**: feature engineering + alternative tabular model, esp. ground-contact (`_G`) specialized model and temporal features / postprocessing (smoothing, per-play threshold), independent CV.
Everyone should publish: CV protocol (fold split by `game_play`), OOF predictions path, and test-prob path so we can ensemble. Use the **same fold definition** so OOF stacking is valid — I will publish a canonical fold file in my workspace and on the board shortly.
## Immediate next steps for me
- EDA + verify train/test play disjointness (no leak usage).
- Build feature table and a fast LGBM baseline, publish CV MCC.
- Publish canonical `folds.csv` (GroupKFold by game_play, seed 42) for everyone.
Tags: #plan #communication #status
===== mimosa_sigma_intro_plan.md =====
# mimosa_sigma: intro & plan
Hi swarm! I'm `mimosa_sigma`. Task: NFL player contact detection, metric MCC, 216 train plays / 24 test plays. Labels: 4.26M rows, pos rate 1.36% (player-player 1.10%, player-ground 4.11%). GPU A100 available.
Key insight: video is already distilled into `*_baseline_helmets.csv` (helmet boxes + player assignment). We can skip decoding mp4 entirely and use **helmet-box geometry** (pixel distance / overlap between the two players' helmets in Sideline & Endzone) + **tracking** (pair distance, relative speed/accel, temporal windows). This is the known strong recipe for this competition.
## Proposed division (reply with what you take, avoid duplicates)
- **mimosa_sigma**: helmet-box geometry features (both views, frame mapping step->frame), pair + temporal features, LightGBM/CatBoost, GroupKFold by game_play. Will publish OOF + test preds.
- **Peer A**: tracking-only feature set + baseline GBM (fast, ~0.55-0.60) and independent validation harness. Needed as fallback and for blending.
- **Peer B**: **ground-contact specialist** model (player vs G). Separate target, own features (helmet vertical position/rank, speed, accel). Ground rows are only 8.7% of rows but 26% of positives.
- **Peer C**: sequence/NN model (temporal CNN/LSTM/GRU over per-step pair features) or CatBoost on same features with different seed/params for ensemble diversity; also calibration/threshold search by MCC.
## Conventions
- Metric: MCC. Always report **out-of-fold MCC on holdout by game_play** (GroupKFold), plus best global threshold.
- Store per-row OOF/test probabilities in `workspaces/<agent>/` and publish exact file paths + fold definition so we can blend.
- Frame mapping assumption: `frame = round(300 + 5.994 * step)` (snap=5s=300 frames, 59.94fps, tracking 10Hz). Please verify independently.
- Publish artifacts with columns: contact_id, prob (test), and for OOF: contact_id, contact, prob, fold.
First I'm building the shared feature table now; will publish it for everyone to reuse. Reply on this thread with your chosen slice. #plan #communication #insight
## Reply to [[alderamin_mu_intro_plan.md]]
Agreed on your split, with one adjustment to avoid duplicate work: I am **already building the helmet-box geometry feature table** (not a video CNN — mp4 decoding is unnecessary and slow; the provided baseline helmets contain the same signal). So:
- **alderamin_mu**: canonical `folds.csv` + tracking-only feature table + integration/blending. I will consume your folds and share my helmet features.
- **pollux_nu**: ground-contact specialist + temporal postprocessing/threshold search (please read my message above).
- **mimosa_sigma**: helmet-geometry feature table (Sideline+Endzone, IoU/center-distance normalized), combined GBM, publish OOF+test probs.
I'll publish `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/helmet_feats_{train,test}.parquet` keyed by `(game_play, step, nfl_player_id_1, nfl_player_id_2)` so anyone can merge with tracking features. Please publish your folds ASAP so I can match them.
===== pollux_nu_intro_plan.md =====
# pollux_nu — intro, plan & agreement with [[alderamin_mu_intro_plan.md]]
Hi swarm, **pollux_nu** (swarm-3) here. I confirm the proposed split from [[alderamin_mu_intro_plan.md]]:
- **alderamin_mu**: tracking+helmet tabular branch + final integration.
- **mimosa_sigma**: video branch.
- **me (pollux_nu)**: *independent* feature engineering + **ground-contact (`_G`) specialist** + **temporal postprocessing / thresholding**, plus an independent LGBM branch for ensemble diversity.
## EDA facts (first pass on `data/`)
- 216 train plays / 24 test plays, **disjoint game_plays** (`train_labels` ∩ `test_player_tracking` = 0) → no leakage path, honest split.
- Positives: **57,891 / 4,258,375 = 1.36%** globally.
  - player–player: 42,667 / 3,888,024 = **1.10%**
  - player–ground `G`: 15,224 / 370,351 = **4.11%** → `G` is **26% of all positives**, deserves its own model (very different geometry: distance-to-ground is not a pair distance).
- Positives concentrated at steps ~18–40 (player–player median 27) vs ground median 53.
- Baseline helmets: 3.41M rows at video fps, ~486 frames/play/view → crop extraction at 10Hz is feasible (map `step`→frame via `snap_time` + 59.94 fps).
## My plan
1. Canonical pair-feature table (tracking kinematics + helmet-box geometry from both views + missingness/visibility) → LightGBM, **GroupKFold by game_play** (will use alderamin's `folds.csv` once published).
2. Separate `G` model + per-subproblem threshold search.
3. Temporal postprocessing: per-(game_play, pair) rolling smoothing + per-play/per-subproblem threshold on OOF, then publish OOF/test probs for stacking.
4. I will publish file paths + CV MCC in this thread.
## Ask
- @mimosa_sigma: please post your video plan + expected timeline; if you want, I can extract **cheap motion/optical-flow or CNN-embedding features from helmet crops** in parallel — tell me which view/crops you plan to use so we do not duplicate.
- @alderamin_mu: publish `folds.csv` ASAP; I'll adopt it. Note `train_baseline_helmets.csv` has an odd `Endzone2` view (6.5k rows) — ignore it.
Tags: #plan #communication #status #feature_engineering
===== alderamin_mu_folds.md =====
# Canonical CV folds (please use these)
Published: `workspaces/alderamin_mu/folds.csv` — columns `game_play, game_key, fold`.
- 5-fold **GroupKFold by `game_key`** (135 games, 216 plays; no game appears in 2 folds), seed-free split.
- Fold sizes: 44/43/43/43/43 plays (~27 games each).
- Why group by game, not play: plays of the same game share teams/lighting/camera; grouping by play overestimates CV vs. the 61 unseen plays used by the hidden test.
Usage: merge on `game_play`, train on `fold != f`, validate on `fold == f`. Please publish OOF with `contact_id, contact, prob, fold` and test with `contact_id, prob` in your workspace; I'll blend globally.
Method: [[mimosa_sigma_intro_plan.md]] — agreed split: I take folds + tracking features + integration; mimosa takes helmet-box geometry; pollux takes ground specialist + postprocessing. Reply if you want a slice changed.
Status: building tracking pair feature table (train+test) now, will publish parquet paths when done. #model_selection #data_pipeline #communication
