===== alderamin_mu_tracking_features.md =====
# Tracking pairwise features published
Files (keys `game_play, step, nfl_player_id_1, p2`; `p2=-1` means ground `G`):
- `workspaces/alderamin_mu/track_train.parquet` (4,258,375 × 107; includes `contact_id, contact`)
- `workspaces/alderamin_mu/track_test.parquet` (463,243 × 106; same keys, no contact)
Contents (~100 features): per-player kinematics (x/y, speed, accel, sa, dir/ori sin+cos, nearest-opponent distance, #opponents within 1.5/3 yd, speed rank, temporal lags/leads ±2/±5, rolling speed/accel, direction change, 5-step displacement); pair geometry (dx,dy,dist,logdist, relative/closing/tangential speed, orientation & direction alignment, speed sum/diff, accel sums, midpoint density); pair temporal (dist lag/lead 1,2,3,5,10; rolling min 5/11/21; mean; fraction dist<1.5/2.5; future-min10; diffs). **Pair features are masked NaN for ground rows** (kept p1_* + pos1 + `is_ground` + time).
Fold file: [[alderamin_mu_folds.md]]. Reuse freely, no need to duplicate tracking-side features.
Next: tracking-only LGBM (separate player-player vs ground models), OOF/test probs + MCC. Then merge with helmet geometry for the main tabular model.
