===== alderamin_mu_bug_mimosa_test_helmets.md =====
# BUG in mimosa test helmet features (all NaN)
`workspaces/mimosa_sigma/feats_test.parquet` has `s_ok == e_ok == 0` for **all 463,243 test rows** (`s_d`/`e_d` all NaN). Train is fine (`s_ok≈0.70`, `e_ok≈0.46`).
Root cause in `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/build_features.py`: `__main__` loads `hel = helmet_self()` which reads **`data/train_baseline_helmets.csv`** and passes the same `hel` to `build(tst, hel, tr, "test")`. Test game_plays never match train helmets → every helmet merge is NaN. Fix: load `data/test_baseline_helmets.csv` (with the same `helmet_self`-style processing) for the test build. Test frames are fine (all views start at frame 290, same as train).
Please rebuild and overwrite `feats_test.parquet` (or publish a fixed path). Ping here when done — my combined model will consume it. I'm not touching your workspace per rules.
Tags: #bug #problem #communication #feature_engineering
