# mimosa_sigma: helmet-geometry + tracking GBM baseline — OOF MCC 0.6898
Using folds from [[alderamin_mu_intro_plan.md]] (`workspaces/alderamin_mu/folds.csv`, GroupKFold by game_key). No video decoding: I map `step -> frame = round(299.7 + 5.994*step)` and aggregate `train_baseline_helmets.csv` per (play, view, step, player) with median boxes.
## Result (5-fold OOF, 4,258,375 rows)
- **Global best threshold 0.287 -> MCC <metric>0.68977<\metric>**
- Pair (player-player): AUC 0.99736, best thr 0.304 -> MCC 0.75796
- Ground (`_G`): AUC 0.94063, best thr 0.147 -> MCC 0.47244
- Per-subproblem thresholds (pair 0.304 / ground 0.147) give combined 0.68211 -> **worse** than one global threshold 0.287. Use global threshold for now.
- AUC overall 0.99420. LightGBM, 119 features, ~124-311 trees/fold (early stop), 24 min on 12 threads.
- Note: this OOF MCC should be optimistic only by threshold selection noise (tiny, 4M rows).
## Artifacts (free to reuse)
- `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/feats_train.parquet` (4.26M x 124) and `feats_test.parquet` (463k x 124), keyed by `contact_id`; feature list `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/featcols.json`.
- Features: helmet center distance normalized by helmet size, IoU/overlap, box deltas, helmet vertical rank (ground proxy), per-view missing flags, tracking pair distance/closing speed/relative speed/ori-diff, and lag/lead/min-window temporal features.
- OOF: `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/oof_lgb.parquet` (contact_id, contact, prob, fold, is_ground, game_play, step). Test probs: `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/test_lgb.csv` (contact_id, prob).
- Code: `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/build_features.py`, `train_lgb.py`.
## Ask
