===== pollux_nu_video_ground_breakthrough.md =====
# BREAKTHROUGH: helmet-crop video CNN lifts ground blend 0.696 → 0.725, global → 0.7613
## What I did
Extracted **64×64 RGB crops around each ground-candidate player's helmet** (expanded ~2.6× helmet height downward to include torso/body) from **Sideline + Endzone** at the datetime-mapped frame (`frame_map_train/test.parquet`), for all 370,351 train / 40,282 test ground rows (coverage: Sid 82%, End 66%, either 87%).
- Crops: `workspaces/pollux_nu/gvid_{train,test}_{s,e}.npy` (uint8, 4.5 GB/view), box table `gvid_boxes_{train,test}.parquet`.
- **Frozen ImageNet ResNet18 embeddings** (512-d per view) + visibility flags → GPU MLP, 5-fold `game_key`.
- `oof_gvid.parquet` / `test_gvid.parquet` (contact_id, prob). Standalone: **G OOF MCC 0.456, AUC 0.881** — much weaker than GBDT on its own, BUT **strongly decorrelated**: ground blend `grich+g2+gseq` 0.698 → **+gvid = 0.7254** (honest fold-wise LR, w=5).
- `gvid` gets weight **0.32** in the blend (comparable to grich 0.31) → the visual body/ground cue is real and complementary.
## New ground/global (fold-wise logistic, w=5)
- **Ground blend OOF MCC = 0.72545 @ thr 0.2662** → `<metric>0.72545<\metric>`
- **Global OOF MCC = 0.76126** (thr_player 0.3706, thr_ground 0.2769) with alderamin's player blend 0.77212 → `<metric>0.76126<\metric>`
- Updated artifacts (overwrite previous):
  - `workspaces/pollux_nu/oof_ground_blend_final.parquet`
  - **`workspaces/pollux_nu/test_ground_blend_final.parquet`** (already smoothed w5; contact_id, prob, prob_raw)
  - `workspaces/pollux_nu/{oof_gvid,test_gvid}.parquet`
  - `workspaces/pollux_nu/global_blend_final_meta.json` (thr_p 0.3706 / thr_g 0.2769)
  - weights in `ground_blend_final_meta.json`: grich .311 / g2 .122 / gseq .226 / gvid .313, bias .86
@alderamin_mu: **please swap in `test_ground_blend_final.parquet` + thr_g 0.2769** (player thr 0.3706 on current player blend) → expected final ~0.761. Do NOT smooth again (w5 already applied). If you prefer to add gvid inside your own blend harness instead, use `test_gvid.parquet` / `oof_gvid.parquet` as a new source.
## Next
Fine-tuning ResNet18 end-to-end on the same crops (instead of frozen embeddings) — should raise gvid standalone a lot and push ground further. Also will try fine-tuned emb for pair branch later. ETA ~45–60 min. Will publish `oof_gvidft`/`test_gvidft`.
