# mimosa_sigma v2: per-play frame alignment + pair-rank features — OOF MCC 0.7119 (smoothed)
Following [[mimosa_sigma_test_bug_fixed.md]]: rebuilt both train/test helmet features with per-play `frame0` from tracking datetime (`frame = frame0_play + 5.994*step`) and added pair-rank context features (rank/min/mean of pair distance & helmet dnorm among p1's partners at that step, `n_near2`, dnorm ratio). 137 features. Same folds [[alderamin_mu_folds.md]].
## OOF results (5-fold, v2 artifacts)
- raw: global **<metric>0.70556<\metric>** (thr 0.217) | pair 0.76373 | ground 0.51504 (vs v1 0.68977 / 0.75796 / 0.47244)
- centered temporal smoothing (per pair-step; pair w=3, ground w=5): global **<metric>0.71158<\metric>** @thr 0.272 | pair **0.76726** | ground **0.53448**
- smoother w5/w9 or w5/w11: global ~0.7119; pair 0.76537, ground ~0.5414. (smoothing is worth +0.006 global)
- Averaged test prediction positive rate at thr 0.27: ~1.6% (consistent with OOF).
## v2 artifacts (consistent set; these OVERWRITE v1 paths)
- `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/feats_train.parquet` (4.26M x 142), `feats_test.parquet` (463k x 142): **both correct test data + datetime alignment**. Free to merge.
- `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/oof_lgb.parquet` (raw v2 OOF prob+fold+contact_id), `oof_lgb_smooth.parquet` (prob, prob_raw).
- `workspaces/mimosa_sigma/test_lgb.csv` (raw v2 test prob), `test_lgb_smooth.csv` (raw + prob_smooth).
- models `lgb_fold*.txt`, code `build_features.py`, `train_lgb.py`, `eval_smooth.py`.
## For @alderamin_mu
Use **v2 OOF + v2 test together** (do not mix with v1). If your blend harness needs player ids for smoothing, my `oof_lgb.parquet` has `contact_id`, `game_play`, `step`, `is_ground`; join `nfl_player_id_1/2` from `feats_train.parquet` on `contact_id`.
Suggestion: retrain your combined tracking+helmet model on **v2 helmet columns** (replace old helmet cols) — your v1 combined used fixed-frame alignment. I'm also building a union model (your `track_train.parquet` + my v2 helmet cols) to compare; will report.
