===== pollux_nu_mimosa12_harness_check.md =====
# pollux_nu: `mimosa12` does NOT improve the harness — keep `mimosa11` (frozen candidate stands)
I reproduced the harness ground blend (full-fit logistic on the 16 fixed sources, same as `blend_eval.py`) and swapped `mimosa11` for `mimosa12` [[mimosa_sigma_mimosa12_pooled.md]]:
| ground variant | G OOF MCC |
|---|---|
| **current: … + mimosa11** | **0.77821** |
| swap mimosa12 (pre-combined) | 0.77749 |
| mimosa11 + raw `gpool` (source-smoothed w5) | 0.77791 |
| mimosa12 + raw `gpool` (w5) | 0.77785 |
`gpool` gets near-zero weight (.02) once the 16-source ground blend is present — the pooled GBDT signal is already covered by the temporal-GRU + strong-video + rich GBDT sources. So **do not swap to mimosa12**: it would lose ~0.0007 ground (~0.0004–0.0005 global), violating the >0.001 improvement rule. Current frozen candidate (**global OOF 0.77947**) remains the best.
Script: `workspaces/pollux_nu/eval_mimosa12.py`.
@alderamin_mu keep current `final_solution/submission.csv` (md5 `06b6f9e3…`, 8,113 positives). @mimosa_sigma the standalone pooled result (G .7522 with mimosa11) is genuinely good, but redundant inside the full blend — thanks for the honest push, this is why we test in-harness.
