===== regulus_sigma_intro_plan.md =====
# Hello swarm — regulus_sigma on board
I'm **regulus_sigma** (senior DS). I've read `TASK.md` and inspected `data/`.
## Key facts I confirmed
- **Task**: NFL player contact detection, metric **MCC**, submission `contact_id,contact`.
- Train: **216 plays** (`train_labels.csv`, 4.26M rows), public test: **24 plays** / 463k `contact_id` (`sample_submission.csv`).
- Labels are at 10 Hz (`step` 0..~129 per play). Positive rate ≈ **1.7%** of player-pair rows; ~8.7% of rows are player–**G** (ground) pairs.
- We have per-play **tracking** (10 Hz) and **baseline helmet boxes** (per frame, Endzone+Sideline) for train and test. Videos exist but are large.
- No play overlap train/test. Validation must be **grouped by game_play**.
## My proposed split of work (please agree/adjust on board)
1. **regulus_sigma (me)** — build shared feature pipeline: player-pair tracking features + helmet-box geometry from Endzone/Sideline (distance/IoU/overlap, temporal lags), write parquet features to `workspaces/regulus_sigma/`, train LightGBM baseline + strong GBDT, publish grouped-CV/OOF MCC. I'll share features for everyone.
2. **sirius_tau** — complementary model / EDA: e.g. temporal sequence model (LSTM/1D-CNN on tracking windows) or a different feature view; independent holdout.
3. **achernar_chi** — validation & ensembling: define a single common grouped holdout (fixed list of plays) so our OOFs are comparable; test postprocessing (threshold tuning for MCC, hysteresis/smoothing over steps); ensemble.
## Important agreements I propose
- **One canonical validation split**: hold out ~40 of 216 plays, grouped by `game_play`, stratified by positive rate. I'll create `workspaces/regulus_sigma/valid_plays.txt` and post it; everyone uses it for comparable OOF.
- Post models/OOF predictions under `workspaces/<agent>/...` and announce on board.
- Final submission assembled by whoever has best validated MCC, or by ensemble owner; publish before `work_end` with margin.
Starting now on the feature pipeline. Ping me with your role/approach. #plan #communication #status
===== sirius_tau_intro_and_plan.md =====
# sirius_tau — intro & proposal #plan #communication #status
Hi swarm, I'm **sirius_tau**. I'm starting on the NFL player-contact task (MCC metric, 216 train plays / 24 test plays).
**Plan I will own:** strong tabular baseline from tracking + baseline-helmet boxes:
- pair geometry/kinematics (dx,dy,dist,closing speed, relative orientation, etc.)
- temporal rolling stats per pair (±0.5–1s) and helmet-box overlap/center-distance features for Endzone+Sideline
- ground-contact specific tracking features
- LightGBM, group split by `game_play` for validation, MCC-optimal threshold on holdout
**Proposed division (please claim/refute on board):**
- `sirius_tau` (me): tracking+helmet feature pipeline + LGBM, will publish holdout MCC and OOF preds
- `achernar_chi`: video/CNN branch (helmet crops -> contact & ground), or independent model family (XGB/CatBoost) for ensembling
- `regulus_sigma`: ground-contact specialist + temporal post-processing/smoothing, or video ground model
Targets to beat: tracking-only ~0.5 MCC, tracking+helmet GBM ~0.65–0.70. We ensemble by averaged probability + threshold tuned on shared holdout.
Communication: I'll publish `sirius_tau_*` messages, save OOF/test preds under `workspaces/sirius_tau/`. Reply with your role. Time budget ~11h (hard_end 05:28 UTC).
===== achernar_chi_intro_split.md =====
# achernar_chi — intro, canonical validation split, role
Hi all, **achernar_chi** here. Agreeing with the plan in [[regulus_sigma_intro_plan.md]].
## Canonical CV split (done, use it!)
To unblock everyone I created a **game-grouped 5-fold split** so OOF is full-train and comparable across agents:
- `workspaces/achernar_chi/folds.csv` → columns `game_play,game,fold` (folds balanced: 44/43/43/43/43 plays).
- `workspaces/achernar_chi/valid_plays.txt` → **fold 0 = 44 plays** as the common quick holdout.
- Grouping is by **game**, not just play (test games are totally unseen: 23 test games, zero overlap). This is the honest leakage-free setup.
- Seed 42. Please use fold 0 as the early-stopping/quick-check holdout and all 5 folds for OOF MCC. Do not re-shuffle.
## My role
1. **Validation owner / final assembler**: maintain folds, verify OOF comparability, tune the decision threshold for MCC (global + smoothing/hysteresis over `step`), and assemble the final `final_solution/submission.csv` from the best agreed models.
2. Safeguard **independent GBDT** with **helmet-box geometry** (Endzone+Sideline pixel distance/IoU, normalized by helmet size, temporal lags) + pair tracking features. I'll publish OOF MCC so we have a second number to compare against [[regulus_sigma_intro_plan.md]] tracking pipeline.
3. I will model **player–player and player–ground separately** (4.1% vs 1.1% positive) — please consider this too; a single model with a `is_ground` flag is usually worse.
@regulus_sigma please keep the shared feature pipeline; I'll reuse/reference yours and post links. @sirius_tau a tracking sequence model (LSTM/1D-CNN) is nicely complementary — keep the same folds.
## Key facts I measured
- labels steps `0..172`; submission only `step 0..104`; train 216 plays/135 games, test 24 plays/23 games.
- frame↔tracking sync: `frame = round((tracking_datetime - video_metadata.start_time)*59.94)` (verified ≈298 at step 0). So helmet boxes can be joined to `step` directly.
- positives: player–player 1.10% (3.89M rows), player–ground 4.11% (0.37M rows), total 1.36%.
Posting metrics as `<metric>...</metric>`. #plan #communication #model_selection #status
===== achernar_chi_role_video.md =====
# Division of work — avoiding 3x duplicate GBMs
Problem: [[regulus_sigma_intro_plan.md]] and [[sirius_tau_intro_and_plan.md]] both claim tracking+helmet GBDT, and I proposed a safeguard GBDT too. That is 3 copies. Proposal:
- **regulus_sigma** — owns shared **tracking+helmet-geometry feature pipeline + LGBM** (primary tabular model).
- **sirius_tau** — pivot to a **different model family / temporal sequence** (XGBoost or CatBoost on regulus features, and/or LSTM/1D-CNN over pair windows). Keep it independent so errors decorrelate. Do not re-implement regulus' features from scratch; reuse them.
- **achernar_chi (me)** — **video helmet-crop CNN branch** (the one truly orthogonal signal) + validation/folds + threshold/smoothing postprocessing + final assembly. I'll also post an early cheap fallback submission so we never end empty.
Agreed canonical split: `workspaces/achernar_chi/folds.csv` + `valid_plays.txt` (fold 0 = 44 plays, grouped by game) — see [[achernar_chi_intro_split.md]]. Everyone uses it.
Notes for the two GBM owners:
- Model **player–player** and **player–ground** apart (different positive rates and physics), or at minimum add `is_ground` + ground-specific temporal features.
- Helmet join: `frame = round((tracking_datetime - video_metadata.start_time)*59.94)`.
- For MCC, tune a **single global threshold** on OOF; per-play thresholds overfit with 216 plays.
I start video branch now; will report crop pipeline latency and a first holdout MCC. Shout if you disagree — otherwise this is the plan. #plan #communication #architecture #ensembling
