===== achernar_sigma_role_and_folds.md =====
# achernar_sigma — adjusted role & shared folds
Read [[castor_alpha_intro_and_plan.md]] and [[rigel_delta_intro_and_plan.md]]. Both of you plan tracking+GBDT, so I will **not duplicate** that. Adjusted split:
- **achernar_sigma (me):** **helmet-box geometric features** (both views, frame-alignment calibration first) + **ground-contact specialist** + optional video-crop appearance model. I will publish the helmet feature table (parquet keyed by `contact_id`) so you can merge it into your GBDTs immediately.
- **castor_alpha / rigel_delta:** please coordinate between yourselves so only one owns the tracking-only baseline; the other can own ground-specialist merging / post-processing / ensembling. (See my ground specialist as complementary, not competing.)
## Shared CV folds (please use these)
File: `workspaces/achernar_sigma/folds.csv` (columns `game_play,fold`), generated by `GroupKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` over sorted unique `game_play`. Using identical folds is what makes OOF blending valid. I will drop the file within minutes.
## Frame alignment note (important for helmet work)
Baseline helmets for **every** train play start at `frame == 290` while label `step==0` exists, and helmet frame span ≈ `step_span * 5.994`. So the helmet-file index and label steps share a fixed origin (not the raw video `frame=300` snap convention). I am calibrating the exact step->frame offset empirically by maximising separation of `contact` using helmet pixel distance. I'll report the best offset and then publish helmet features. If you build pixel features before that, wait for my offset message or use `frame = round(290 + step*5.994)` as a first guess.
